A quick 4-ingredient Instant Pot casserole that makes a hearty breakfast, brunch, or dinner. Frozen hash brown cubes and savory ham steaks are layered, pressure-cooked in seasoned broth, and topped with a blanket of gooey melted cheese.

*Adapted from [Instant Pot Official Recipes](https://recipes.instantpot.com/recipe/cheesy-ham-and-potato-casserole/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 cup chicken or beef broth
- 2 lbs frozen unseasoned hash brown cubes (southern-style hash browns)
- 2 frozen thin boneless ham steaks (8 oz each)
- 1 ½ teaspoons minced fresh sage (or ½ teaspoon dried sage)
- 1 teaspoon fresh thyme leaves (or ½ teaspoon dried thyme)
- 1 teaspoon onion powder
- ¼ teaspoon cayenne pepper (optional, for gentle warmth)
- 2 cups shredded Swiss or sharp cheddar cheese (8 oz)

## Instructions

1. **Warm the Broth:** Pour the 1 cup of chicken or beef broth into the Instant Pot inner pot. Turn on the **Sauté** function and heat just until wisps of steam begin rising from the liquid (a very gentle low simmer—do not boil vigorously so you don't lose liquid needed for pressure). Turn off the Sauté function.
2. **Layer the Casserole:** Make an even layer of half of the frozen hash brown potato cubes in the bottom of the pot. Break or cut the frozen ham steaks into thirds (or smaller pieces) and lay them across the potato layer. Scatter the remaining hash brown cubes evenly over the ham. Evenly sprinkle the sage, thyme, onion powder, and optional cayenne across the top of the potatoes.
3. **Pressure Cook:** Lock the lid onto the cooker and ensure the steam release valve is set to the **Sealing** position. Select **Pressure Cook (Manual)** on **HIGH** pressure for 4 minutes with the Keep Warm function turned off.
4. **Quick Release:** When the 4-minute cooking cycle finishes, immediately perform a quick pressure release. Once all steam has vented and the float valve drops, carefully unlock and remove the lid.
5. **Melt the Cheese and Serve:** Evenly scatter the 2 cups of shredded cheese across the top of the hot potatoes. Set the lid askew over the cooker and let stand for 5 minutes so the residual steam thoroughly melts the cheese into a bubbly crust. Serve hot by the big spoonful.

## Notes

- **Potato Type:** Unseasoned cubed hash brown potatoes (often labeled "Southern Style Hash Browns") work best because they maintain their distinct cube shape under pressure cooking without turning into mush.
- **Cheese Options:** Swiss cheese lends a nutty, fondue-like flavor, while sharp cheddar or Colby Jack gives a classic casserole profile.
